comments.body:
@participant6 

> I don't think my logs are huge. I checked the kafka monitor and there are only 200+ data being generated per second.

@reporter said that the throughput is only about 200 "data" (? logs? lines?) per second for the issue to occur. So the write_ml.sh will sleep accordingly to print 200 lines/sec. I let it run with 1000 lines/sec over last night and there was no increase in CPU load over time.

@participant6 please don't get me wrong. I also see this behaviour one _**some**_ Fluent Bit instances (even though the log rate is very low ~ 20-200 logs/sec). Look at the number of chunks and running tasks.
![Bildschirmfoto 2024-09-25 um 12 32 20](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0ec3d76a-63e0-45fd-867f-fc9e19b35ed1)

I could not find the reason for it, yet.

@participant5 Do you have any clue where these many tasks are coming from? There's almost no load on the pipeline at the moment of the screenshot.
